                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Owol7",
                  "name": "--gd-font-size-<name>, -",
                  "fill": "#76756F",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "--gd-font-size-<name>, --gd-line-height-<name>  ·  fontSize / lineHeight / fontWeight / letterSpacing in tokens.ts. One family carries both roles and both scripts: Onest is neutral enough for a dense list row and has enough character at 32px to head a page, so the split between UI and display is weight and tracking, not a second typeface. Cyrillic is part of the family, not a fallback — users write in Russian and a Latin job title sits next to a Russian description inside one line. Letter spacing and font weight are TS-only: css.ts does not emit them.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.5,
                  "fontFamily": "Onest",
                  "fontSize": 12,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
